course: dictionary
lesson: 14514
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Peppery can mean spicy, and it can mean quick to get angry. Look at the words around it to find the right one. «The soup was peppery, so I drank a glass of water.» Water helps when your mouth is hot, so peppery must mean hot and spicy here.
explain: «Dad went peppery when the car would not start.» Cars do not taste of anything, so this sentence is about feelings, not food. Peppery means quick to get angry, or bad-tempered. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the whole sentence?
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it in. Does «The soup was bad-tempered» make sense? No, so the taste meaning is right. Check the other way too. Peppery is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a peppery curry or a peppery old man.
fact: Peppery means tasting hot and spicy, full of pepper.
fact: Peppery also means quick to get angry; bad-tempered.
fact: «Rocket and watercress taste peppery» because their leaves have a sharp, hot taste.
fact: In Alice in Wonderland, the Duchess's kitchen is full of pepper, so everyone sneezes, and the Duchess is peppery in temper too.
fact: Peppery can be used of people: «a peppery old colonel» is a man who shouts a lot.
exercise: «The curry was so peppery that Sam had to drink a whole glass of milk.» What does peppery mean here? | Sweet and sticky | *Tasting hot and spicy | Quick to get angry | Cold and wet
exercise: «Grandma became peppery when the boys broke her vase.» What does peppery mean here? | Very quiet and calm | Happy and giggly | Tasting hot and spicy | *Quick to get angry; bad-tempered
exercise: «Add rocket to the salad, because its leaves are peppery.» What does this tell you about rocket? | Its leaves are soft and cold | *Its leaves taste hot and sharp | Its leaves are very large | Its leaves make people angry
test: «The old colonel was peppery, and he shouted at the children for running.» What does peppery mean here? | Shy and quiet | Hot and spicy | Very tired | *Bad-tempered and quick to shout
test: «The chilli is more peppery than the soup.» What does more peppery mean here? | Angrier | Sweeter | *Spicier, hotter to taste | Colder
exam: «Mum said the stew was peppery, and later Dad was peppery too after a long day.» Which two meanings of peppery are used in this sentence? | Sweet and sticky, and very tall | *Tasting hot and spicy, and quick to get angry | Happy and calm, and full of fun | Cold and wet, and very quiet
